      image: "cat_gear.png",
      clues: [
        { value: 200, clue: "Riders over 250cc must carry proof of this mandatory government safety check, called shaken in Japanese.", response: "What is the (periodic) vehicle inspection?", note: "Shaken (車検) is Japan's compulsory periodic inspection; bikes over 250cc need it, 250cc-and-under are exempt.", source: { label: "Japanistry — Owning a motorcycle in Japan", url: "https://www.japanistry.com/motorcycle-ownership-japan/" }, image: "shaken_inspection.png" },
        { value: 200, clue: "Because it's the largest displacement exempt from the shaken inspection, bikes of THIS size are wildly popular for budget touring.", response: "What is 250cc?", note: "250cc is the biggest size that avoids shaken, making it the most popular touring class.", source: { label: "Japanistry — Owning a motorcycle in Japan", url: "https://www.japanistry.com/motorcycle-ownership-japan/" }, image: "250cc_touring.png" },
        { value: 400, clue: "Every motorcycle on a public road must carry this compulsory liability insurance, known as jibaiseki, covering injury you cause to others.", response: "What is compulsory (liability) insurance?", note: "Jibaiseki / JCI is mandatory for all vehicles and covers bodily injury to others, not your own bike.", source: { label: "MLIT — Compulsory Automobile Liability Insurance", url: "https://www.mlit.go.jp/jidosha/jibaiseki/en/faq/index.html" }, image: "compulsory_insurance.png" },
        { value: 400, clue: "A 50cc moped wears one of these in white, a 90cc bike in yellow, and a 125cc bike in pink, so the color signals engine size at a glance.", response: "What is a license plate?", note: "For small bikes (≤125cc), plate color shows displacement: white ≤50, yellow 51-90, pink 91-125cc.", source: { label: "Wikipedia — Vehicle registration plates of Japan", url: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vehicle_registration_plates_of_Japan" }, image: "plate_colors.png" },
        { value: 400, clue: "Even sub-250cc bikes that skip shaken must keep these two black-rubber parts in good condition to stay roadworthy.", response: "What are the tires?", note: "Exempt bikes must still be roadworthy — tires and brakes maintained.", source: { label: "Japanistry — Owning a motorcycle in Japan", url: "https://www.japanistry.com/motorcycle-ownership-japan/" }, image: "motorcycle_tires.png" },
        { value: 600, clue: "To use expressway toll gates you can't reuse a car's ETC box; you need a weatherproof unit made specifically for these vehicles.", response: "What are motorcycles?", note: "Bikes need a dedicated two-wheel ETC unit; a car unit lacks the water/vibration resistance and won't match the registration.", source: { label: "NEXCO East (E-NEXCO) FAQ", url: "https://www.cs3.e-nexco.co.jp/faq/s/article/219" }, image: "motorcycle_etc_unit.png" },
        { value: 600, clue: "After its first check at three years, an over-250cc bike must repeat the shaken inspection on this recurring interval.", response: "What is every two years?", note: "Over-250cc bikes get their first shaken at 3 years, then every 2 years.", source: { label: "Wikipedia — Motor-vehicle inspection (Japan)", url: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motor-vehicle_inspection_(Japan)" }, image: "shaken_interval.png" },
        { value: 600, clue: "A bike-specific ETC unit can't be self-installed off the shelf; it must be set up at one of these authorized dealers.", response: "What is an authorized installation shop?", note: "Motorcycle ETC units may only be bought and fitted at authorized two-wheel ETC setup dealers.", source: { label: "GO! ETC (ITS Promotion)", url: "https://www.go-etc.jp/motorcycle/index.html" }, image: "etc_setup_shop.png" },
        { value: 800, clue: "Ride without your compulsory jibaiseki insurance and you face up to a year in jail or a fine up to this many hundred-thousand yen.", response: "What is 500,000 yen (five)?", note: "No compulsory insurance: up to 1 year or up to ¥500,000, plus 6 points and suspension.", source: { label: "MLIT — Penalties for driving without liability insurance", url: "https://www.mlit.go.jp/jidosha/jibaiseki/en/about/punish/index.html" }, image: "insurance_penalty.png" },
        { value: 800, clue: "Foreigners assume the leaf-shaped wakaba beginner mark goes on their bike, but that sticker is legally tied to this different class of vehicle.", response: "What is an (ordinary) car?", note: "The shoshinsha/wakaba beginner mark is required for new ordinary-CAR licenses, not motorcycles.", source: { label: "PLAZA HOMES — Driving stickers in Japan", url: "https://www.realestate-tokyo.com/living-in-tokyo/driving/driving-stickers/" }, image: "wakaba_mark.png" },
        { value: 800, clue: "A bike of 250cc or less skips shaken, but to register one you still get this 'light-vehicle' document an ETC shop asks for.", response: "What is a light-vehicle registration certificate?", note: "Sub-250cc bikes use a 軽自動車届出済証 (light-vehicle certificate); over-250cc use a 車検証.", source: { label: "SBS Powers — ETC for motorcycle", url: "https://www.powers-mc.com/english/eng_etc.html" }, image: "light_vehicle_cert.png" },
        { value: 1000, clue: "Get caught riding uninsured and, on top of any fine, you take six of these against your license — enough to trigger a suspension.", response: "What are demerit (penalty) points?", note: "Riding without compulsory insurance adds 6 demerit points, enough to suspend the license.", source: { label: "MLIT — Penalties for driving without liability insurance", url: "https://www.mlit.go.jp/jidosha/jibaiseki/en/about/punish/index.html" }, image: "demerit_points.png" },
        { value: 1000, clue: "Even with an inspected, insured bike, failing to keep this proof-of-insurance paper ON you is a separate offense, fined up to ¥300,000.", response: "What is the compulsory-insurance certificate?", note: "Not carrying the jibaiseki certificate is a separate offense punishable by up to ¥300,000.", source: { label: "MLIT — Penalties for driving without liability insurance", url: "https://www.mlit.go.jp/jidosha/jibaiseki/en/about/punish/index.html" }, image: "insurance_certificate.png" },
        { value: 1000, clue: "'Shaken' is a contraction; its full form translates to this multi-word English phrase describing the whole system.", response: "What is the automobile inspection registration system?", note: "車検 abbreviates 自動車検査登録制度, the 'automobile inspection registration system.'", source: { label: "Wikipedia — Motor-vehicle inspection (Japan)", url: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motor-vehicle_inspection_(Japan)" }, image: "shaken_system.png" },
      ],
